1
00:04:25,714 --> 00:04:31,714
You see them on the street. You watch them on TV. You might even vote for one this
fall. You think they're people just like you. You're wrong. Dead wrong.

2
00:08:51,428 --> 00:08:57,428
They Live is a science fiction, action, thriller
film directed by John Carpenter.

3
00:13:17,142 --> 00:13:23,142
A lone drifter stumbles upon a unique pair of sunglasses that reveal aliens are systematically gaining
control of the Earth by masquerading as humans and lulling the public into submission.

4
00:17:42,857 --> 00:17:48,857
John Nada, played by Roddy Piper.

5
00:22:08,571 --> 00:22:14,571
Frank Armitage, played by Keith David.

6
00:26:34,285 --> 00:26:40,285
Holly Thompsen, played by Meg Foster.

7
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Drifter, played by George Buck Flower.

8
00:35:25,714 --> 00:35:31,714
Gilbert, played by Peter Jason.

9
00:39:51,428 --> 00:39:57,428
Street Preacher, played by Raymond St. Jacques.

10
00:44:17,142 --> 00:44:23,142
They Live is a 1988 American science fiction action horror film written, directed, and
scored by John Carpenter, and starring Roddy Piper, Keith David, and Meg Foster.

11
00:48:42,857 --> 00:48:48,857
It was based on the 1963 short story "Eight
O'Clock in the Morning" by Ray Nelson.

12
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:14,571
Having acquired the film rights to the story prior to the production of They Live, Carpenter used the story as
the basis for the screenplay's structure, which he wrote under the pseudonym "Frank Armitage".

13
00:57:34,285 --> 00:57:40,285
Carpenter has stated that the themes of They Live stemmed from his
dissatisfaction with the economic policies of then-U.S.

14
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
President Ronald Reagan, as well as what Carpenter saw as increasing
commercialization in both popular culture and politics.

15
01:06:25,714 --> 01:06:31,714
They Live was a minor success upon release, debuting at
number 1 at the North American box office.

16
01:10:51,428 --> 01:10:57,428
It initially received negative reviews from critics, who lambasted its social commentary, writing, and acting;
however, it later gained a cult following and experienced a significantly more favorable critical reception.

17
01:15:17,142 --> 01:15:23,142
It is now regarded by many as one of Carpenter's best films.

18
01:19:42,857 --> 01:19:48,857
The film has also entered the pop culture lexicon, notably having a lasting
effect on street art (particularly that of Shepard Fairey).

19
01:24:08,571 --> 01:24:14,571
The film explores themes of capitalism, dystopia,
villainess, alien, social commentary.

20
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking and intense.
